    "text": "<p>For real numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>,</mo></math> if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#948;</mi><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant, then the v